=== the tile graph = K_n minus the base path: cut/cycle dimensions ===
  n    m  comps  cut=n-1  cycle=m-n+1    2^cycle
  4    3      1        3            0          1
  5    6      1        4            2          4
  6   10      1        5            5         32
  7   15      1        6            9        512
  8   21      1        7           14      16384
  9   28      1        8           20    1048576

=== star group vs isomorphism, by exhaustive enumeration ===
n=4: m=3  star-group dim=3 (cut dim n-1=3)  orbits=1 (predicted 2^(m-n+1)=1)  iso classes=4
      star-orbits refine iso-classes? False   iso-classes refine star-orbits? True
      3-cycle count constant on ISO classes? True   on STAR orbits? False
n=5: m=6  star-group dim=4 (cut dim n-1=4)  orbits=4 (predicted 2^(m-n+1)=4)  iso classes=12
      star-orbits refine iso-classes? False   iso-classes refine star-orbits? False
      3-cycle count constant on ISO classes? True   on STAR orbits? False
n=6: m=10  star-group dim=5 (cut dim n-1=5)  orbits=32 (predicted 2^(m-n+1)=32)  iso classes=56
      star-orbits refine iso-classes? False   iso-classes refine star-orbits? False
      3-cycle count constant on ISO classes? True   on STAR orbits? False
n=7: m=15  star-group dim=6 (cut dim n-1=6)  orbits=512 (predicted 2^(m-n+1)=512)  iso classes=456
      star-orbits refine iso-classes? False   iso-classes refine star-orbits? False
      3-cycle count constant on ISO classes? True   on STAR orbits? False

VERDICT
  (1) <stars> = the CUT space of the tile graph (dim n-1, tile graph connected).
      Quotient = dual of the CYCLE space, #orbits = 2^(m-n+1) -- exact match.
      So point adjacency DOES produce invariants: the F_2 holonomies (cycle parities).
  (2) NOT the merged metagraph and NOT a refinement: for n>=5 neither partition
      refines the other. The star quotient is TRANSVERSE to isomorphism.
  (3) Tournament cycle invariants (3-cycle count) descend to ISO classes but NOT
      to star orbits; the star-orbit class is a TILING function that does not
      descend to iso classes. The two invariant systems are transverse.
